      "version": 5,
      "src": "/android-2024-10-11",
      "notes": "canonical x86_64 base (Bliss 16.9.7). Versionless filename mirrors base_arm; lineage tracked in 'version' + 'changelog' (files were base-v5.* until 2026-07-09).",
      "changelog": {
        "1": "pristine Bliss OS 16.9.7 x86_64 (2026-07-05)",
        "2": "v1 + custom loading screen + kiosk system app (2026-07-05)",
        "3": "v2 + kiosk with black wallpaper; silent boot moved host-side (2026-07-06)",
        "4": "v3 + pre-installed game com.roblox.client as system app - PRODUCTION (2026-07-06)",
        "5": "updated kiosk (Lock Task lockdown + boot/RAM trims) (2026-07-06)"
      }
    },
    "arm": {
      "type": "arm-uefi",
      "base_disk": "base_arm_v2.qcow2",
      "system": "base_arm_system_rooted.qcow2",
      "data": "base_arm_data_rooted.qcow2",
      "efivars": "base_arm_efivars.fd",
      "src": "https://github.com/jqssun/android-lineage-qemu (LineageOS 23.2 arm64, virtio_arm64only)",
      "notes": "arm64/UEFI base (LineageOS 23.2). v2 = branded + silent + insecure_adb + Roblox baked in. base_arm.qcow2 (v1) is kept because existing account overlays are still COW-backed by it. [rooted]",
      "version": 3,
      "changelog": {
        "1": "pristine LineageOS 23.2 arm64 (jqssun virtio) + kiosk/device-owner provisioned pair",
        "2": "v1 + Omni loading screen (product/media), silent boot (quiet/loglevel=0), GRUB menu hidden (no LineageOS logo/countdown), androidboot.insecure_adb=1 (adb reachable on a fresh boot - without it every new account stalls on 'Allow USB debugging?'), and Roblox pre-installed as a system app in /product/app/Roblox with its arm64 native libs (2026-07-17)",
        "3": "v2 + persist.sys.zram_enabled=1 baked into /product/etc/build.prop, which turns on the zram swap the image already declares in /vendor/etc/fstab.virtio (zramsize=50%, lz4) via the swapon_all trigger in /vendor/etc/init/zram.rc. Measured: lz4 compresses ~3x, the safe balloon cap drops 1536 -> 1024 MB, and a production (non-rooted) instance holds Roblox at that cap with zero kills. base_arm_system_zram.qcow2 is a ~1 MB COW overlay of base_arm_system.qcow2, which is untouched - revert by pointing 'system' back at it. (2026-08-05) NOTE: zstd was tried on top of this (v4) and REVERTED - it is worse. At the 896 MB cap lz4 holds with zero kills, zstd killed the game with 3 mem-pressure kills, and boot went 0.8 min -> 5+ min (timing out `omni start`). zstd wins on compression RATIO but loses on THROUGHPUT, and on one vCPU it is reclaim LATENCY that decides whether an instance survives pressure. Do not retry without more vCPUs."
      },
      "rooted": true,
      "root_manifest": {
        "magisk_version": "v30.7",
        "frida_version": "17.15.4",
        "frida_port": 27142,
        "rooted_system": "base_arm_system_rooted.qcow2",
        "rooted_data": "base_arm_data_rooted.qcow2"
      }
    }
  },
